  "transpose": false,
  "notes": "Source table on page 92 provides Pre-Retirement Mortality Rates for ages 20-60 in 5-year bands, printed as percentages (e.g. 0.04% = 0.0004). Post-retirement and post-disability rates are not provided as sample tables in this document (only table references to Pub-2010 tables). Consequently, the 'Death_Prob' column is constructed using only the pre-retirement rates (ages 20-64). For ages 65 and above, no source rates exist in the document, so the target rows are empty. The weights for the group_weighted operation use the Active Member counts by age (page 16) for both Male and Female sources, effectively averaging the sex-specific rates. The '60' age bin in the source table is open-ended [60, null], but active membership is negligible beyond age 69, so the effective weight is clipped to [60, 69] in the mapping logic.",
  "unavailable": false
}